course: dictionary
lesson: 16095
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and watermark is one of them. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. These words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Hold the note up to the light and you can see the watermark.» The clues are hold it up to the light and see. So a watermark here is a faint picture pressed into paper, which shows up when light shines through it.
explain: «The photo had a faint watermark in the corner, so nobody could copy it.» Here the clues are photo and copy. A watermark is a faint logo or word put over a picture to show who owns it.
explain: «The flood left a watermark on the bridge, showing how high the water had risen.» The clue is how high the water had risen. This watermark is a high-water mark, a mark that shows how far the water reached. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A watermark is a faint picture or pattern in paper that you can see when you hold it up to the light.
fact: A watermark can also be a faint logo or word on a digital picture or document, showing who owns it.
fact: A high-water mark is a mark showing how high water has reached, and it can also be called a watermark.
fact: Banknotes have watermarks as one of their security features, which help stop forged money.
fact: As a verb, to watermark means to put a watermark on paper or a picture.
exercise: «Hold the note up to the light to see the watermark.» Where would you see a watermark in this sentence? | *Faint in the paper, when you hold it up to the light | Written in big capital letters on the cover | Printed on the outside of a tin | Hidden inside a box
exercise: «The photo had a faint watermark in the corner.» Why might someone put a watermark on a photo? | To make the photo smaller | *To show who owns it | To stop the photo from being printed | To make the colours brighter
exercise: «The old bridge had a watermark showing how high the river had risen in the flood.» What does watermark mean in this sentence? | A type of pen | A loud noise from the river | A picture pressed into paper | *A mark showing how high water has reached
test: «Banknotes have a watermark to help stop them being forged.» What is the watermark for? | To make the note easier to tear | To show the value of the bank | *To help show the note is real | To make the note heavier
test: Ella says a watermark is always a loud sound. What is the best reply? | Yes, it is a kind of tune played on a piano | *No, a watermark is a faint picture or mark | No, it is a kind of fish that lives in rivers | Yes, it is a loud sound that you can hear from far away
exam: Which sentence uses watermark as a verb? | *The artist will watermark each photo before it goes online | The high-water mark is on the old wall | The note had a watermark in the corner | The watermark was faint in the paper
